                        "glosses": [
                            "One who ordains or establishes; a director."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "890ea9fd-bbe2-43da-b362-7ef7d4e11804",
                                "sense_id": "0792c9e7-2e0f-3dfc-b1c1-7f9c837faf5f",
                                "text": "if nature and her ordinator, God, deny health, how unvaluable are their riches, how unavailable their projects!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b741c97f-78f1-42bd-b5ea-37601e599f69",
                                "sense_id": "0792c9e7-2e0f-3dfc-b1c1-7f9c837faf5f",
                                "text": "The plan which has proved most satisfactory is something like this: One teacher, the class ordinator, is made responsible for the general discipline and progress of a class."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c92d699a-ff24-4f3d-bba9-30cc7a8eb1bd",
                                "sense_id": "0792c9e7-2e0f-3dfc-b1c1-7f9c837faf5f",
                                "text": "God is ordinator no less than creator; if he is naturarum bonarum creator, he is also malarum uoluntatum ordinator; if human wills make a bad use of good things , he in turn makes a good use even of evil wills."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "796c896d-69a1-4bb0-ab10-25c4b99d2119",
                                "sense_id": "0792c9e7-2e0f-3dfc-b1c1-7f9c837faf5f",
                                "text": "This is the only synod in America to have an ordinator, and it is here that the Lutheran resembles the Episcopalian. But the ordinator is not consecrated—that is not a Danish custom—his office resembling that of the superintendents in Germany."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "20e2ead8-e09f-44b6-9b6a-81ccb8799854",
                                "sense_id": "0792c9e7-2e0f-3dfc-b1c1-7f9c837faf5f",
                                "text": "During the social hour, he went to the office of the assistant ordinator, a weasel-faced man wearing the dark blue Interchange uniform as if it were a privilege."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
